author: builder
title: 'M1.13 slice 1: Gnomon.app (macOS) — double-click wrapper, signed and notarized'
summary: packages/gnomon-wrapper ships as a Tauri 2.12.4 app that spawns 'gnomon up --wrapper' with a clean env, reads the launch grant on a private stdout pipe (gnomon-wrapper-channel:v1), verifies the bundle pin, its own hello serverSig (ed25519-dalek) and the served bytes natively, then navigates to the one loopback origin. No page IPC, locked navigation, devtools debug-only, empty entitlements. Close hides, Cmd-Q stops the kernel. Built, Developer-ID signed, notarized (Accepted) and stapled.
symbols_touched:
  - '#gnomon-wrapper'
  - '#gnomon-up'
  - '#dev-launch'
  - '#gui'
  - '#web-endpoint'
commit: 60989ae1
learnings:
  - 'tauri 2.11.5 does not compile against the tauri-runtime 2.12 cargo resolves: pin 2.12.4 + tauri-build 2.7.3'
  - 'Node child stdio pipes on macOS are socketpairs (fstat isSocket) while Rust Command uses real FIFOs: a channel check must accept both'
  - invoke_system with a keyless stub removes the only page-visible copy of the Tauri invoke key
  - 'the app topology inverted mid-task: the app is the parent and the kernel child writes the grant on its stdout pipe'
  - 'a GUI change moves GUI_BUNDLE_HASH which the wrapper compiles in: rebuild the app with the GUI'
